OpenIDE-Module-Name: TGraph Demo
OpenIDE-Module-Requires: org.openide.windows.WindowManager
OpenIDE-Module-Short-Description: TGraph is a database designed for temporal graph data.
OpenIDE-Module-Long-Description: TGraphDB is a Neo4j compatiable database that manage temporal property (property value change history).This Gephi plugin shows the power of TGraph database. TGraph is a database designed to manage temporal graph data. This plugin comes with TGraph's kernel, and implement a tiny traffic-query-system on a specific data set. It implements several algorithms: Heatmap (aggregate) of traffic status, Earliest arrive path, Historical query of traffic status and so on.
    Start with our 3-minutes video tutorial: https://youtu.be/nbWa_5OL3GU or http://mashuai.buaa.edu.cn/TGraphdemo.avi
    For more help, see https://github.com/TGraphDB/gephi-demo/tree/TGraphDemo/modules/TGraphDemo
    To get more info of TGraph Database, see http://dx.doi.org/10.1145/2983323.2983335
OpenIDE-Module-Display-Category: Tool
